WEBVTT

00:00:06.364 --> 00:00:07.532
Lord Bern?

00:00:11.036 --> 00:00:12.245
Perhaps once.

00:00:13.163 --> 00:00:15.540
But I'm no longer
deserving of that title.

00:00:17.376 --> 00:00:18.585
Is he one of the seven?

00:00:26.426 --> 00:00:27.511
Your face.

00:00:28.804 --> 00:00:31.181
You remind me of a king
I once loved well.

00:00:32.182 --> 00:00:33.183
That man was my father.

00:00:34.559 --> 00:00:36.478
(voice trembling) Oh, my Lord.

00:00:36.561 --> 00:00:38.063
Please forgive me.

00:00:38.146 --> 00:00:40.565
No, please. Please.

00:00:40.649 --> 00:00:43.026
(horse neighs in distance)

00:00:43.693 --> 00:00:45.404
WOMAN: No!

00:00:45.487 --> 00:00:47.322
(people shouting)

00:00:47.406 --> 00:00:49.324
(screaming, shouting)

00:00:51.410 --> 00:00:52.702
GIRL: Mummy!

00:00:52.786 --> 00:00:54.287
Please!

00:00:56.039 --> 00:00:56.957
Mummy!

00:00:57.040 --> 00:00:58.750
Get back!

00:00:58.834 --> 00:01:00.877
-No!
-Mummy!

00:01:00.961 --> 00:01:02.129
Stay with Daddy!

00:01:02.212 --> 00:01:04.506
Don't worry! I'll find you!

00:01:04.589 --> 00:01:06.091
Mummy!

00:01:09.428 --> 00:01:11.012
(screaming, shouting in distance)

00:01:17.436 --> 00:01:18.603
WOMAN: No!

00:01:18.687 --> 00:01:20.147
Where are they taking them?

00:01:20.230 --> 00:01:22.274
Keep watching.

00:01:25.152 --> 00:01:27.487
(thunder rumbling)

00:01:34.870 --> 00:01:38.540
(eerie voices moaning, whispering)

00:01:45.505 --> 00:01:47.549
(people screaming)

00:01:51.678 --> 00:01:53.430
CASPIAN: What happened?

00:01:53.513 --> 00:01:55.515
BERN: It's a sacrifice.

00:01:56.683 --> 00:01:58.935
-Where did they go?
-No one knows.

00:01:59.811 --> 00:02:03.231
The mist was first seen in the East.

00:02:03.315 --> 00:02:07.027
Reports of fishermen and sailors
disappearing out at sea.

00:02:07.486 --> 00:02:09.613
We lords made a pact

00:02:09.696 --> 00:02:12.449
to find the source
of the mist to destroy it.

00:02:13.241 --> 00:02:14.409
They each set sail...

00:02:15.702 --> 00:02:17.120
...but none came back.

00:02:22.167 --> 00:02:25.712
You see, if they don't sell
you to the slave traders,

00:02:25.796 --> 00:02:28.090
you're likely to be fed to the mist.

00:02:28.173 --> 00:02:29.758
EDMUND: We have to find Lucy.

00:02:30.675 --> 00:02:31.885
Before it's too late.

00:02:31.968 --> 00:02:34.012
-MAN: I bid 60!
-MAN 2: I bid 80!

00:02:34.096 --> 00:02:35.722
One hundred for the little lady!

00:02:35.806 --> 00:02:37.265
One hundred and twenty!

00:02:37.349 --> 00:02:39.017
On hundred fifty!

00:02:39.101 --> 00:02:40.936
MAN: Any more bids?

00:02:41.019 --> 00:02:42.646
(men murmuring)

00:02:44.398 --> 00:02:45.482
Sold!

00:02:45.565 --> 00:02:46.942
(screams)

00:02:47.025 --> 00:02:50.112
Come on, move! Move!

00:02:50.195 --> 00:02:53.990
MAN: And now, for this fine specimen,

00:02:54.074 --> 00:02:56.034
who'll kick off the bidding?

00:02:56.743 --> 00:02:58.829
Come on, now.

00:02:58.912 --> 00:03:02.416
He may not look like much,
but, uh, he's strong.

00:03:02.499 --> 00:03:05.127
RYNELF: Yeah, he's strong all right.
Smells like the rear end of a Minotaur.

00:03:05.210 --> 00:03:06.920
(laughter)

00:03:07.003 --> 00:03:08.880
That is an outrageous lie!

00:03:09.673 --> 00:03:12.384
I won the school hygiene award
two years running.

00:03:12.467 --> 00:03:13.677
-(laughter)
-Mm!

00:03:13.760 --> 00:03:16.054
Come on, someone make a bid!

00:03:16.138 --> 00:03:18.140
REEPICHEEP:
I'll take them off your hands.

00:03:18.223 --> 00:03:20.058
I'll take them all off your hands!

00:03:20.142 --> 00:03:21.393
For Narnia!

00:03:21.476 --> 00:03:22.602
-Narnia!
-Narnia!

00:03:22.686 --> 00:03:24.104
(men yelling, shouting)

00:03:25.939 --> 00:03:27.649
Guards! Guards!

00:03:27.733 --> 00:03:28.984
(swords clanging)

00:03:30.610 --> 00:03:32.946
(groaning, yelling)

00:03:34.865 --> 00:03:36.158
(screams)

00:03:37.993 --> 00:03:40.328
(grunting, yelling)

00:03:44.291 --> 00:03:46.209
Thanks, Reep. I knew you'd come.

00:03:46.293 --> 00:03:47.586
Your Highness. Yah!

00:03:52.799 --> 00:03:53.800
(screams)

00:03:54.843 --> 00:03:56.303
Get the keys!

00:03:58.764 --> 00:03:59.973
(roars)

00:04:00.057 --> 00:04:01.183
(screams)

00:04:04.061 --> 00:04:05.353
Keys!

00:04:05.437 --> 00:04:06.646
(screams)

00:04:12.986 --> 00:04:15.030
(yelling)

00:04:15.113 --> 00:04:16.239
(gasps)

00:04:17.991 --> 00:04:19.534
(grunting)

00:04:21.495 --> 00:04:22.579
(screams)

00:04:22.662 --> 00:04:24.289
(clamoring)

00:04:41.473 --> 00:04:44.810
Oh, you're a boat in a magical land.
Can't you row yourself?

00:04:57.948 --> 00:04:59.533
Whoa...

00:04:59.616 --> 00:05:02.202
(grunting)

00:05:02.285 --> 00:05:03.995
(gasps)

00:05:04.079 --> 00:05:06.790
Oh, God.
I hope that wasn't the British Consul.

00:05:06.873 --> 00:05:08.667
(cheering, applause)

00:05:08.750 --> 00:05:11.461
-Your Majesty. Your Majesty!
-Hold it!

00:05:11.545 --> 00:05:13.588
My wife was taken just this morning.

00:05:13.672 --> 00:05:14.881
-Daddy!
-It's all right, Drinian.

00:05:14.965 --> 00:05:16.383
I beg you, take me with you.

00:05:16.466 --> 00:05:17.843
WOMAN: Gael!

00:05:17.926 --> 00:05:20.721
-I want to come.
-No, Gael, stay with your aunt.

00:05:20.804 --> 00:05:22.264
I'm a fine sailor.

00:05:22.347 --> 00:05:24.307
Been on the seas my whole life.

00:05:24.391 --> 00:05:25.934
Of course, you must.

00:05:26.017 --> 00:05:27.561
-Thank you.
-But Daddy...

00:05:27.644 --> 00:05:29.187
Have I ever not come back?

00:05:31.314 --> 00:05:32.357
Now, be good.

00:05:33.483 --> 00:05:35.193
(cheering, applause continues)

00:05:38.321 --> 00:05:41.324
My king! My king!

00:05:45.954 --> 00:05:48.498
This was given to me by your father.

00:05:48.582 --> 00:05:50.834
I hid it safely in a cave all these years.

00:05:50.917 --> 00:05:52.711
That's an old Narnian sword.

00:05:52.794 --> 00:05:54.463
It's from your Golden Age.

00:05:54.546 --> 00:05:59.551
There are seven such swords,
gifts from Aslan to protect Narnia.

00:06:00.802 --> 00:06:03.263
Your father entrusted them to us.

00:06:04.139 --> 00:06:05.849
Here, take it.

00:06:09.311 --> 00:06:10.937
And may it protect you.

00:06:17.944 --> 00:06:20.155
(crowd cheering)

00:06:20.822 --> 00:06:21.990
CASPIAN: Thank you, my lord.

00:06:23.200 --> 00:06:24.868
And we shall find your lost citizens.

00:06:29.539 --> 00:06:30.582
Edmund.

